                    Text#927 [page-title] "Russia and Ukraine widen strike campaign as attacks on energy grid and refineries intensify"
                    Pressable#928 [reader-versions] label="Versions" (press)
                      View#929
                        Text#930 "Version 175 of 175 · Nov 26, 2026"
                        Image#931
                    View#932
                    View#933
                      Text#934 [reader-block-b2] (contextmenu)
                        Text#935 "Russia launched 317 long-range attack drones at Ukraine overnight on Nov 8–9, according to Ukraine's Air Force "
                        Text#936 [reader-cite-ref-cbffc4035653] " 1 " label="Source 1" (press)
                        Text#937 ". "
                        Text#938 "Russian attacks injured 28 people across Ukraine over the past day, regional authorities said "
                        Text#939 [reader-cite-ref-30fd32d1faa7] " 1 " label="Source 1" (press)
                        Text#940 ". "
                        Text#941 "Ukrainian drones hit two Russian targets in the same period, and at least four people were killed across both countries."
                    View#942
                      Text#943 [reader-block-b3] (contextmenu)
                        Text#944 "A further overnight wave from the evening of Nov 9 was smaller: Ukraine's air defenses said they downed 135 of 162 Russian drones "
                        Text#945 [reader-cite-ref-6d25850a7831] " 2 " label="Source 2" (press)
                        Text#946 ". "
                        Text#947 "In Kherson oblast, Ukrainian authorities reported one person killed and six injured in the past day from drone attacks, artillery shelling and airstrikes "
                        Text#948 [reader-cite-ref-510b2eb3fc50] " 3 " label="Source 3" (press)
                        Text#949 "."
                    View#950
                      Text#951 [reader-block-b4] (contextmenu)
                        Text#952 "On November 10, Ukraine’s air defenses neutralized 124 Russian drones and 14 S8000 Bandrol jet-powered loitering munitions "
                        Text#953 [reader-cite-ref-0175dee57d05] " 4 " label="Source 4" (press)
                        Text#954 "."
                    View#955
                      Text#956 [reader-block-b5] (contextmenu)
                        Text#957 "Strikes continued into Nov 10: two people were killed in a Russian attack on a civilian enterprise in the city of Ladyzhyn in Vinnytsia oblast, according to the regional governor, Natalia Zabolotna, and the city council secretary, with three days of mourning declared "
                        Text#958 [reader-cite-ref-32fa427570c3] " 5 " label="Source 5" (press)
                        Text#959 "."
                    View#960
                      Text#961 [reader-block-b6] (contextmenu)
                        Text#962 "Russian forces struck Zaporizhzhia twice during the day on Nov 10, injuring four people and sparking fires, and hit a residential apartment block, according to the oblast governor, Mykhailo Semikin "
                        Text#963 [reader-cite-ref-37f84c0ab75c] " 6 " label="Source 6" (press)
                        Text#964 ". "
                        Text#965 "In the Dnipropetrovsk region, attacks on energy infrastructure left parts of Dnipro and Kamianske without power "
                        Text#966 [reader-cite-ref-d428c8aaaa11] " 7 " label="Source 7" (press)
                        Text#967 "."
                    View#968
                      Text#969 [reader-block-b7] (contextmenu)
                        Text#970 "Over the past day, Russian forces launched 1,107 strikes on 54 settlements in Zaporizhzhia oblast, with one person killed and fifteen injured in attacks on Zaporizhzhia and the Zaporizhzhia district, according to Ukrinform "
                        Text#971 [reader-cite-ref-7a71e8ce13d7] " 8 " label="Source 8" (press)
                        Text#972 " "
                        Text#973 "."
                    View#974
                      Text#975 [reader-block-b8] (contextmenu)
                        Text#976 "Russian forces struck Kryvyi Rih with drones targeting critical infrastructure, leaving the city partially without electricity, according to Oleksandr Vilkul, head of the Kryvyi Rih Defense Council "
                        Text#977 [reader-cite-ref-975c0e9ff4ee] " 9 " label="Source 9" (press)
                        Text#978 ". "
                        Text#979 "Water and sewage systems are being stabilized on generators, and heating is expected to be harder to maintain "
                        Text#980 [reader-cite-ref-a74a7c4524f4] " 9 " label="Source 9" (press)
                        Text#981 ". "
                        Text#982 "Damaged buildings included apartment blocks, schools and kindergartens "
                        Text#983 [reader-cite-ref-7cf67180285e] " 9 " label="Source 9" (press)
                        Text#984 ". "
                        Text#985 "In the Zaporizhzhia district, six people were injured in an attack that damaged four private homes, an apartment and a shop, according to Babel "
                        Text#986 [reader-cite-ref-c6cb05007d81] " 10 " label="Source 10" (press)
                        Text#987 "."
                    View#988
                      Text#989 [reader-block-b9] (contextmenu)
                        Text#990 "A Ukrainian commander says Russian forces are striking bridges and dams to isolate Zaporizhzhia, as pressure on Ukraine's defenses in the oblast grows "
                        Text#991 [reader-cite-ref-9860b44b9cd4] " 11 " label="Source 11" (press)
                        Text#992 "."
                    View#993
                      Text#994 [reader-block-b10] (contextmenu)
                        Text#995 "Two people were killed and at least four injured when a Russian strike hit critical infrastructure in Dnipro, starting a fire, the oblast governor, Hancha, said; explosions were also heard in Mykolaiv "
                        Text#996 [reader-cite-ref-6b2093eb2507] " 12 " label="Source 12" (press)
                        Text#997 "."
                    View#998
                      Text#999 [reader-block-b11] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1000 "Pravda reported that humanitarian conditions in 34 settlements in Kherson oblast had become critical, as bad as in Oleshky "
                        Text#1001 [reader-cite-ref-b2b5e53df275] " 13 " label="Source 13" (press)
                        Text#1002 "."
                    View#1003
                      Text#1004 [reader-block-b12] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1005 "Pravda reported that four people were injured in attacks on civilians in Zhytomyr oblast "
                        Text#1006 [reader-cite-ref-7c70e04f559f] " 14 " label="Source 14" (press)
                        Text#1007 ". "
                        Text#1008 "Pravda also reported that two Russian drone-launched missiles entered Moldova's airspace "
                        Text#1009 [reader-cite-ref-0b5ec5df1b38] " 15 " label="Source 15" (press)
                        Text#1010 "."
                    View#1011
                      Text#1012 [reader-block-b13] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1013 "Russia launched a double missile strike on Kharkiv overnight into Nov 11, according to Mayor Ihor Terekhov; the attack hit the Industrialnyi and Saltivskyi districts and consequences were still being assessed "
                        Text#1014 [reader-cite-ref-fdb8e1d735ca] " 16 " label="Source 16" (press)
                        Text#1015 " "
                        Text#1016 " "
                        Text#1017 ". "
                        Text#1018 "In the Saltivskyi district, one person was injured in the strike; apartment buildings and a garage cooperative were damaged, according to Ukrinform "
                        Text#1019 [reader-cite-ref-ae091dd7d759] " 17 " label="Source 17" (press)
                        Text#1020 " "
                        Text#1021 ". "
                        Text#1022 "The Kharkiv regional head also reported two people were killed in the Saltivskyi district strike "
                        Text#1023 [reader-cite-ref-5f7088f5e302] " 18 " label="Source 18" (press)
                        Text#1024 " "
                        Text#1025 ". "
                        Text#1026 "A missile strike also triggered a major fire in Kharkiv "
                        Text#1027 [reader-cite-ref-a3cbe110c966] " 19 " label="Source 19" (press)
                        Text#1028 "."
                    View#1029
                      Text#1030 [reader-block-b14] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1031 "In Kyiv, a private house was damaged in the Darnytskyi district during a Russian attack, according to Ukrinform "
                        Text#1032 [reader-cite-ref-c39d0ecd7dbe] " 20 " label="Source 20" (press)
                        Text#1033 ". "
                        Text#1034 "A drone strike on a nine-story apartment building in the Solomianskyi district set fire to floors three through six and partially destroyed the fifth floor "
                        Text#1035 [reader-cite-ref-d99f6cf5d4a7] " 21 " label="Source 21" (press)
                        Text#1036 ". "
                        Text#1037 "Mayor Vitali Klitschko said emergency services were on the scene and that there was preliminary partial destruction on the fifth floor "
                        Text#1038 [reader-cite-ref-9ac1ab9033c2] " 22 " label="Source 22" (press)
                        Text#1039 " "
                        Text#1040 ". "
                        Text#1041 "A woman was killed in Kyiv in the Russian attack, with five people reported injured "
                        Text#1042 [reader-cite-ref-214845ebe9da] " 23 " label="Source 23" (press)
                        Text#1043 " "
                        Text#1044 "."
                    View#1045
                      Text#1046 [reader-block-b15] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1047 "Russia attacked Kyiv with ballistic missiles hours after peace talks ended "
                        Text#1048 [reader-cite-ref-62e9e91f46a0] " 24 " label="Source 24" (press)
                        Text#1049 ". "
                        Text#1050 "Multiple rounds of explosions were reported in the city after 1 a.m. "
                        Text#1051 [reader-cite-ref-deca621b7ee5] " 24 " label="Source 24" (press)
                        Text#1052 ". "
                        Text#1053 "Suspilne correspondents also reported explosions in Mykolaiv "
                        Text#1054 [reader-cite-ref-40d17db7d834] " 25 " label="Source 25" (press)
                        Text#1055 "."
                    View#1056
                      Text#1057 [reader-block-b16] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1058 "Russia also struck a retail facility in the city of Kropyvnytskyi, in central Ukraine "
                        Text#1059 [reader-cite-ref-1a8ffc3be0a6] " 26 " label="Source 26" (press)
                        Text#1060 "."
                    View#1061
                      Text#1062 [reader-block-b17] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1063 "On November 12, four people were killed and six injured in Russian strikes on Kramatorsk, in the Donetsk region "
                        Text#1064 [reader-cite-ref-61777ee166dc] " 27 " label="Source 27" (press)
                        Text#1065 ". "
                        Text#1066 "Confectioner Kateryna Seledtsova reported that front-line Kramatorsk had been without electricity for 15 days "
                        Text#1067 [reader-cite-ref-031b9b92962b] " 28 " label="Source 28" (press)
                        Text#1068 ". "
                        Text#1069 "A Russian drone also hit a residential apartment block in Rivne, causing a fire and leaving five people injured "
                        Text#1070 [reader-cite-ref-cb548158dce1] " 29 " label="Source 29" (press)
                        Text#1071 ". "
                        Text#1072 "Overnight into November 13, air-raid alerts for a ballistic threat were declared in almost all regions of Ukraine, with local authorities calling residents to shelters; the all-clear was announced around 02:06 "
                        Text#1073 [reader-cite-ref-3169e77cec17] " 30 " label="Source 30" (press)
                        Text#1074 " "
                        Text#1075 "."
                    View#1076
                      Text#1077 [reader-block-b18] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1078 "Russia's Ministry of Defense said four people were killed in a major Ukrainian drone barrage "
                        Text#1079 [reader-cite-ref-e377e8271308] " 31 " label="Source 31" (press)
                        Text#1080 "."
                    View#1081
                      Text#1082 [reader-block-b19] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1083 "Footage published on November 13 also showed a drone striking a car on a road in Odesa "
                        Text#1084 [reader-cite-ref-21e00c6d5c1e] " 32 " label="Source 32" (press)
                        Text#1085 "."
                    View#1086
                      Text#1087 [reader-block-b20] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1088 "Three people — two women and one man — were killed and one seriously wounded when a Russian drone strike hit a food-storage warehouse in the port city of Odesa, the city's military administration said; it was the third strike on that logistics enterprise "
                        Text#1089 [reader-cite-ref-30be68f64610] " 33 " label="Source 33" (press)
                        Text#1090 ". "
                        Text#1091 "On the Russian side, the Kirishi refinery in Russia's Leningrad region was set on fire in a Ukrainian drone attack and one woman was killed by falling drone debris, Governor Aleksandr Drozdenko said; Ukraine's military chief of staff said Ukraine also hit the Morozov explosives and fuel plant near St Petersburg "
                        Text#1092 [reader-cite-ref-41618c4dedb2] " 34 " label="Source 34" (press)
                        Text#1093 " "
                        Text#1094 ". "
                        Text#1095 "The Spy's Dossier reported that a November 9 attack on Kirishnefteorgsintez damaged key units including the ELOU-AVT-2, AT-1, AT-6, fuel oil processing complex, Parex-2 and two water supply units, and that plant operations were suspended "
                        Text#1096 [reader-cite-ref-a23557903162] " 35 " label="Source 35" (press)
                        Text#1097 ". "
                        Text#1098 "Separately, explosions rocked Russia's Novgorod region early Monday; a monitor suggested the Defense Forces likely attacked the 123rd Aviation Repair Plant, which services military transport aircraft "
                        Text#1099 [reader-cite-ref-63d1f4e31139] " 36 " label="Source 36" (press)
                        Text#1100 " "
                        Text#1101 "."
                    View#1102
                      Text#1103 [reader-block-b21] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1104 "In Vinnytsia, two women were injured in a Russian attack that damaged residential buildings and a kindergarten, city mayor Serhii Morhunov said "
                        Text#1105 [reader-cite-ref-a1c29f06d5f8] " 37 " label="Source 37" (press)
                        Text#1106 " "
                        Text#1107 "."
                    View#1108
                      Text#1109 [reader-block-b22] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1110 "Reports also emerged of powerful explosions and electronic warfare systems being activated in Russia's Adygea region, along with a fire on a high-rise roof "
                        Text#1111 [reader-cite-ref-32618c1229ab] " 38 " label="Source 38" (press)
                        Text#1112 " "
                        Text#1113 [reader-cite-ref-d394a635a21d] " 39 " label="Source 39" (press)
                        Text#1114 "."
                    View#1115
                      Text#1116 [reader-block-b23] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1117 "Moscow Mayor Sergey Sobyanin claimed that over a hundred drones had been shot down en route to the Russian capital, grounding flights at regional airports "
                        Text#1118 [reader-cite-ref-81b4ddf940ad] " 40 " label="Source 40" (press)
                        Text#1119 ". "
                        Text#1120 "Eyewitness footage from the scene appears to show flames emanating from the Lukoil-Volgogradneftepererabotka refinery, one of Russia's largest oil refineries, while a Rostov-on-Don production facility was also reported in flames "
                        Text#1121 [reader-cite-ref-4946b3930b06] " 41 " label="Source 41" (press)
                        Text#1122 ". "
                        Text#1123 "The governor of Rostov Oblast confirmed an attack on the region and fires at warehouses following a kamikaze drone strike "
                        Text#1124 [reader-cite-ref-71b002cd2e7c] " 42 " label="Source 42" (press)
                        Text#1125 ". "
                        Text#1126 "OSINT channel Exilenova reported that explosions continued in the area of Lukoil-Volgogradneftepererabotka and that the Volgograd Refinery was forced to suspend its work "
                        Text#1127 [reader-cite-ref-aa1d3d5e839a] " 43 " label="Source 43" (press)
                        Text#1128 " "
                        Text#1129 [reader-cite-ref-d051c6f911a9] " 44 " label="Source 44" (press)
                        Text#1130 ". "
                        Text#1131 "Exilenova suggested that Ukrainian forces may have changed tactics, sending a large number of drones to strike the entire industrial zone of each refinery rather than just processing units, in order to disable capacity for as long as possible "
                        Text#1132 [reader-cite-ref-96584b17c24d] " 45 " label="Source 45" (press)
                        Text#1133 ". "
                        Text#1134 "The channel also reported this was at least the 13th attack on the Volgograd refinery since the start of the full-scale war "
                        Text#1135 [reader-cite-ref-360b093454c8] " 46 " label="Source 46" (press)
                        Text#1136 ". "
                        Text#1137 "Exilenova later reported that the refinery was still burning in Volgograd "
                        Text#1138 [reader-cite-ref-0cf42c4ae830] " 47 " label="Source 47" (press)
                        Text#1139 "."
                    View#1140
                      Text#1141 [reader-block-b24] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1142 "Censor.net reported that drones attacked the Volgograd oil refinery on November 12, where a fire broke out "
                        Text#1143 [reader-cite-ref-d43584278496] " 48 " label="Source 48" (press)
                        Text#1144 "."
                    View#1145
                      Text#1146 [reader-block-b25] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1147 "Defense manufacturer Fire Point reported that Ukrainian drone strikes knocked out 36% of Russia's total oil refining capacity in less than two weeks, hitting at least nine major refineries between Oct. "
                        Text#1148 "30 and Nov. "
                        Text#1149 "11; the combined annual processing capacity of the plants hit exceeds 120 million metric tons of crude oil "
                        Text#1150 [reader-cite-ref-311dc79e2c7b] " 49 " label="Source 49" (press)
                        Text#1151 " "
                        Text#1152 ". "
                        Text#1153 "Reuters separately assessed that attacks since late October have reduced Russia's operational refining capacity by roughly 30% "
                        Text#1154 [reader-cite-ref-34afd8d75f05] " 49 " label="Source 49" (press)
                        Text#1155 ". "
                        Text#1156 "The figure also ends a late-October pause: a Kyiv Independent op-ed reports that, with Washington pressing Kyiv, Ukraine went almost two weeks without hitting Russian refineries, though it kept carrying out attacks on other targets inside Russia "
                        Text#1157 [reader-cite-ref-a959eb17888f] " 50 " label="Source 50" (press)
                        Text#1158 "."
                    View#1159
                      Text#1160 [reader-block-b26] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1161 "Meduza reported that regional governor Andrey Bocharov said Ukrainian drones attacked the Volgograd region, sparking a fire at an industrial facility and causing fatalities "
                        Text#1162 [reader-cite-ref-d61c0850e448] " 51 " label="Source 51" (press)
                        Text#1163 "."
                    View#1164
                      Text#1165 [reader-block-b27] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1166 "Ukrinform reported that National Guard drone crews have struck more than 316,000 enemy targets since the start of the full-scale invasion, almost 150,000 of which were destroyed "
                        Text#1167 [reader-cite-ref-c8f9bcd874c6] " 52 " label="Source 52" (press)
                        Text#1168 ". "
                        Text#1169 "Separately, the National Guard said drones and ground robots delivered nearly 6,200 tons of cargo, evacuated 499 service members and laid 143,000 mines and engineering obstacles "
                        Text#1170 [reader-cite-ref-de890dce336c] " 53 " label="Source 53" (press)
                        Text#1171 "."
                    View#1172
                      Text#1173 [reader-block-b28] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1174 "Katimsya also reported that drones traveled about 3,000 kilometers to strike the Omsk refinery, and that the port and oil terminal at Ust-Luga in Russia were still burning "
                        Text#1175 [reader-cite-ref-8bb1744c476f] " 54 " label="Source 54" (press)
                        Text#1176 " "
                        Text#1177 ". "
                        Text#1178 "The SBU reported that its agents together with other SOU units hit the Novatek-Ust-Luga terminal, damaging several 30,000-ton tanks, the Ust-Luga Oil terminal, and the Faktor terminal, as well as a Buyan-M missile ship carrying Kalibr and Oniks missiles "
                        Text#1179 [reader-cite-ref-d5a2b527979f] " 55 " label="Source 55" (press)
                        Text#1180 " "
                        Text#1181 ". "
                        Text#1182 "Exilenova reported that explosions were still being heard in Omsk on the seventh hour of the attack "
                        Text#1183 [reader-cite-ref-19a056f0f4bb] " 56 " label="Source 56" (press)
                        Text#1184 "."
                    View#1185
                      Text#1186 [reader-block-b29] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1187 "Reuters reported that four people were killed in a Ukrainian drone strike on an industrial zone in Russia's Volgograd region, according to an official "
                        Text#1188 [reader-cite-ref-a41b2e27f214] " 57 " label="Source 57" (press)
                        Text#1189 "."
                    View#1190
                      Text#1191 [reader-block-b30] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1192 "OSINT channel Exilenova reported that a Ukrainian airstrike on Russia's Volgograd region killed four people "
                        Text#1193 [reader-cite-ref-22e1a6dcf39d] " 58 " label="Source 58" (press)
                        Text#1194 " and that not only the port, tankers, turntables and an airplane and a ship burned in the Leningrad region, but also Nebo-U, Sopka-2 and 40B6 systems "
                        Text#1195 [reader-cite-ref-0115acd4fa88] " 59 " label="Source 59" (press)
                        Text#1196 "."
                    View#1197
                      Text#1198 [reader-block-b31] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1199 "OSINT channel Exilenova reported that an explosive device went off in a Lexus car under the driver "
                        Text#1200 [reader-cite-ref-2a40b66d75b9] " 60 " label="Source 60" (press)
                        Text#1201 " and that a road bridge over the Mius River on the R-280 \"Novorossiya\" highway was destroyed by an FP-2 drone "
                        Text#1202 [reader-cite-ref-eafc28d4514b] " 61 " label="Source 61" (press)
                        Text#1203 "."
                    View#1204
                      Text#1205 [reader-block-b32] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1206 "OSINT account GlobalsConflicts reported that a Russian soldier was killed in a car explosion in Saint Petersburg "
                        Text#1207 [reader-cite-ref-1fb64f5a6395] " 62 " label="Source 62" (press)
                        Text#1208 "."
                    View#1209
                      Text#1210 [reader-block-b33] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1211 "DW reported that a second car bomb exploded in Moscow in two days, targeting an exiled Ukrainian political aide "
                        Text#1212 [reader-cite-ref-cbe6b01a3fe6] " 63 " label="Source 63" (press)
                        Text#1213 "."
                    View#1214
                      Text#1215 [reader-block-b34] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1216 "Russia's Ministry of Defense said it carried out a massive overnight strike on military factories across Ukraine, including Kyiv, where one person was killed and five injured "
                        Text#1217 [reader-cite-ref-5cfa4aa6a122] " 64 " label="Source 64" (press)
                        Text#1218 "."
                    View#1219
                      Text#1220 [reader-block-b35] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1221 "EU foreign policy chief Kaja Kallas warned that talking with Russia about the security architecture would walk into the traps Moscow is setting, diverting attention from the absence of a ceasefire "
                        Text#1222 [reader-cite-ref-ad62ce607a07] " 65 " label="Source 65" (press)
                        Text#1223 "."
                    View#1224
                      Text#1225 [reader-block-b36] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1226 "Russia's deputy permanent representative to the United Nations, Anna Evstigneeva, told colleagues that Russia was targeting facilities that directly provide products for Ukraine's armed forces and said, \"We are doing this in a very precise and cautious manner, exercising restraint, because we value the lives of people\" "
                        Text#1227 [reader-cite-ref-e73c5abaecf2] " 66 " label="Source 66" (press)
                        Text#1228 " "
                        Text#1229 "."
                    View#1230
                      Text#1231 [reader-block-b37] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1232 "A Russian attack on an industrial facility in Zaporizhzhia on November 13 killed a man who had been trapped under the rubble, according to the acting head of the oblast military administration, Mykhailo Semikin "
                        Text#1233 [reader-cite-ref-9eae9ce7c3fd] " 67 " label="Source 67" (press)
                        Text#1234 ". "
                        Text#1235 "Earlier that morning, Russian forces struck a residential area in Zaporizhzhia, killing a teenager and injuring four people "
                        Text#1236 [reader-cite-ref-0c102451f5fd] " 67 " label="Source 67" (press)
                        Text#1237 "."
                    View#1238
                      Text#1239 [reader-block-b38] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1240 "Ukraine's State Emergency Service said Russian forces struck a five-story building in Zaporizhzhia, injuring 13 people including five children "
                        Text#1241 [reader-cite-ref-ede51772c990] " 68 " label="Source 68" (press)
                        Text#1242 ". "
                        Text#1243 "In Odesa, the emergency service reported that a Russian strike killed two people and injured seven "
                        Text#1244 [reader-cite-ref-857abeb23443] " 68 " label="Source 68" (press)
                        Text#1245 "."
                    View#1246
                      Text#1247 [reader-block-b39] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1248 "At least three people were killed and more than 20 injured in Russian strikes on Ukraine on November 13, according to a Mastodon report citing a conflicts monitor "
