                      Text#1579 [reader-block-b82] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1580 "Der Spiegel reported that Russia is systematically destroying Kyiv's electricity supply, and described daily life for one Kyiv family without regular power as a struggle to wash laundry, charge phones and even take the dog for a walk "
                        Text#1581 [reader-cite-ref-4da98082fd03] " 144 " label="Source 144" (press)
                        Text#1582 "."
                    View#1583
                      Text#1584 [reader-block-b83] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1585 "OSINT account RosHlopok reported that Ukrainian drones hit three Russian targets on the night of Nov 14—Proletarsky, Shcherbinichi and Churovichi—and claimed offline refining capacity of 110 Mt per year out of 324 Mt "
                        Text#1586 [reader-cite-ref-88f67ede95fd] " 145 " label="Source 145" (press)
                        Text#1587 " "
                        Text#1588 ". "
                        Text#1589 "OSINT channel Exilenova also claimed that on the night of Nov 13 Ukrainian forces struck the Volgograd \"Lukoil\" oil refinery, damaging all primary oil-processing installations and destroying six tanks with the fire area exceeding 3,500 square meters "
                        Text#1590 [reader-cite-ref-23e6da44efdc] " 146 " label="Source 146" (press)
                        Text#1591 " "
                        Text#1592 "."
                    View#1593
                      Text#1594 [reader-block-b84] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1595 "Ukrainian drones reportedly attacked the Kuibyshev Oil Refinery in Syzran, Samara region; the Rosneft-owned facility has a nominal refining capacity of 7 million metric tons of crude oil per year, about 2.6% of Russia's total refining volume "
                        Text#1596 [reader-cite-ref-d371d85abf9a] " 147 " label="Source 147" (press)
                        Text#1597 " "
                        Text#1598 [reader-cite-ref-1f7a174a3cb5] " 148 " label="Source 148" (press)
                        Text#1599 ". "
                        Text#1600 "The same OSINT channel reported the refinery \"going up in flames\" and said people were asked not to post footage or look out the windows because air defense was repelling the attack "
                        Text#1601 [reader-cite-ref-db1a41001108] " 149 " label="Source 149" (press)
                        Text#1602 ". "
                        Text#1603 "The channel later posted footage of \"today's attack on the Syzran Oil Refinery, broadcast live\" and said two refineries were down — and a third in question — in the Samara region in a single night "
                        Text#1604 [reader-cite-ref-8b890ea38852] " 150 " label="Source 150" (press)
                        Text#1605 "."
                    View#1606
                      Text#1607 [reader-block-b85] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1608 "Meduza reported that Ukrainian drones attacked Russia's Samara region overnight on Nov 24–25, killing one person and setting two Rosneft oil refineries on fire "
                        Text#1609 [reader-cite-ref-536115a985b3] " 151 " label="Source 151" (press)
                        Text#1610 ". "
                        Text#1611 "OSINT monitoring account Analytics reported that on the night of Nov 25 Ukrainian drones attacked both the Kuibyshev Oil Refinery and the Syzransky refinery in the Samara region, with photos and videos circulating from the scene and no official damage reports yet "
                        Text#1612 [reader-cite-ref-f9f0ae397d4a] " 152 " label="Source 152" (press)
                        Text#1613 "."
                    View#1614
                      Text#1615 [reader-block-b86] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1616 "Five regions in Ukraine faced power outages after overnight strikes "
                        Text#1617 [reader-cite-ref-2dfada968a6b] " 153 " label="Source 153" (press)
                        Text#1618 ". "
                        Text#1619 "A Ukrainian official says attacks on the Zaporizhzhia and Dnipropetrovsk regions damaged a number of energy sites "
                        Text#1620 [reader-cite-ref-b5b3fb2b0e73] " 154 " label="Source 154" (press)
                        Text#1621 "."
                    View#1622
                      Text#1623 [reader-block-b87] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1624 "Ukraine's foreign minister told Putin to end the war if he wants Kyiv to stop attacking Russian refineries, after Putin said retaliation was \"inevitable\" "
                        Text#1625 [reader-cite-ref-a6439cce7f9c] " 155 " label="Source 155" (press)
                        Text#1626 "."
                    View#1627
                      Text#1628 [reader-block-b88] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1629 "Moscow and Kyiv traded infrastructure attacks as allies argued over Ukraine's actions in Libya, with Poland saying it is puzzled by the lack of a US response to Russian incursions in its airspace "
                        Text#1630 [reader-cite-ref-d9e32f7834ff] " 156 " label="Source 156" (press)
                        Text#1631 "."
                    View#1632
                      Text#1633 [reader-block-b89] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1634 "An OSINT account reported that Russian strikes killed seven in Ukraine while Kyiv hit three refineries "
                        Text#1635 [reader-cite-ref-4767860da46d] " 157 " label="Source 157" (press)
                        Text#1636 "."
                    View#1637
                      Text#1638 [reader-block-b90] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1639 "Ukraine said five Russian military jets were hit in an airfield strike; the Savasleyka airfield hosts aircraft used by Russia to launch hypersonic missiles and glide bombs at Ukraine "
                        Text#1640 [reader-cite-ref-dada06e50000] " 158 " label="Source 158" (press)
                        Text#1641 "."
                    View#1642
                      Text#1643 [reader-block-b91] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1644 "Pravda reported that drones attacked several oil refineries in Russia, sparking fires "
                        Text#1645 [reader-cite-ref-05548d92ebe2] " 159 " label="Source 159" (press)
                        Text#1646 ". "
                        Text#1647 "Pravda also reported that the number of people injured in a Russian strike on civilians in Zaporizhzhia rose to 50, including children "
                        Text#1648 [reader-cite-ref-77c79f5734b0] " 160 " label="Source 160" (press)
                        Text#1649 ". "
                        Text#1650 "Pravda's daily tally said Russia lost 2,091 troops and 15 artillery systems over the past day "
                        Text#1651 [reader-cite-ref-5f6e85cc248a] " 161 " label="Source 161" (press)
                        Text#1652 "."
                    View#1653
                      Text#1654 [reader-block-b92] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1655 "Overnight Russian drone strikes hit Bila Tserkva and Volyn oblast, killing one person and injuring five, according to Ukrainian media reports relayed by a Mastodon news account "
                        Text#1656 [reader-cite-ref-35a849e3adc9] " 162 " label="Source 162" (press)
                        Text#1657 " "
                        Text#1658 [reader-cite-ref-52e2a27b84d2] " 163 " label="Source 163" (press)
                        Text#1659 ". "
                        Text#1660 "In Dnipro, emergency responders set up additional assistance points for residents amid a difficult electricity supply situation "
                        Text#1661 [reader-cite-ref-788fe166700c] " 164 " label="Source 164" (press)
                        Text#1662 "."
                    View#1663
                      Text#1664 [reader-block-b93] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1665 "A fresh Russian attack left parts of Odesa without power, with consumers in the Prymorskyi and Peresypskyi districts cut off and critical infrastructure operating with disruptions, according to energy company DTEK "
                        Text#1666 [reader-cite-ref-081639afaf5d] " 165 " label="Source 165" (press)
                        Text#1667 "."
                    View#1668
                      Text#1669 [reader-block-b94] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1670 "Ukrinform reported that the number of people injured in a Russian combined strike on Zaporizhzhia rose to seven "
                        Text#1671 [reader-cite-ref-604bc99add6a] " 166 " label="Source 166" (press)
                        Text#1672 ". "
                        Text#1673 "A Pravda report relayed by a Mastodon news account said Ukrainian intelligence destroyed a Russian aerospace reconnaissance system in Smolensk Oblast "
                        Text#1674 [reader-cite-ref-0bc212326ac3] " 167 " label="Source 167" (press)
                        Text#1675 ". "
                        Text#1676 "Another Pravda-linked report said one person was killed and five others injured in a Russian attack on civilians in Zhytomyr Oblast "
                        Text#1677 [reader-cite-ref-8da84210b985] " 168 " label="Source 168" (press)
                        Text#1678 ". "
                        Text#1679 "Ukraine's chargé d'affaires in the US, Denys Sienik, said the parties involved still have not explained who decided to restrict Starshield's operation in Ukraine, adding that the restrictions increase danger for civilians "
                        Text#1680 [reader-cite-ref-cc6e26477fd7] " 169 " label="Source 169" (press)
                        Text#1681 "."
                    View#1682
                      Text#1683 [reader-block-b95] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1684 "A Ukrainian official said attacks on the Zaporizhzhia and Dnipropetrovsk regions damaged a number of energy sites, as five regions faced power outages after overnight strikes "
                        Text#1685 [reader-cite-ref-a340625d63bf] " 170 " label="Source 170" (press)
                        Text#1686 "."
                    View#1687
                      Text#1688 [reader-block-b96] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1689 "Air alerts reported drone activity over Kharkiv and Zaporizhzhia regions, with shelling reported in Balakliia "
                        Text#1690 [reader-cite-ref-233f55ef6d3e] " 171 " label="Source 171" (press)
                        Text#1691 ". "
                        Text#1692 "Drone attacks were also confirmed over Zhytomyr, Dnipropetrovsk and Odesa regions, including in Malyn, Dnipro and Odesa/Chornomorsk "
                        Text#1693 [reader-cite-ref-d1dd51d8f8ea] " 172 " label="Source 172" (press)
                        Text#1694 "."
                    View#1695
                      Text#1696 [reader-block-b97] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1697 "A video report described multiple fires at two Rosneft refineries as Ukraine targeted Russian energy infrastructure "
                        Text#1698 [reader-cite-ref-ed0d83fc8403] " 173 " label="Source 173" (press)
                        Text#1699 ". "
                        Text#1700 "Ukraine's General Staff reported that at the Savasleyka air base, \"уражено три російські літаки МіГ-31 і два Су-34\" "
                        Text#1701 [reader-cite-ref-f6f87d56b2de] " 174 " label="Source 174" (press)
                        Text#1702 "."
                    View#1703
                      Text#1704 [reader-block-b98] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1705 "A Russian overnight attack on Ukraine's energy and gas sites halted a thermal power plant and sparked a large fire at a gas facility "
                        Text#1706 [reader-cite-ref-243a90eaee0b] " 175 " label="Source 175" (press)
                        Text#1707 ". "
                        Text#1708 "Power to the Zaporizhzhia nuclear plant was cut for the 17th time this year "
                        Text#1709 [reader-cite-ref-1041a5743fd8] " 175 " label="Source 175" (press)
                        Text#1710 "."
                    View#1711
                      Text#1712 [reader-block-b99] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1713 "Ukrainian forces reported hitting five aircraft at Savasleyka airfield — three MiG-31 and two Su-34 jets — and attacking the Kuibyshev and Syzran oil refineries in Russia's Samara oblast overnight "
                        Text#1714 [reader-cite-ref-36d1edf0433f] " 176 " label="Source 176" (press)
                        Text#1715 ". "
                        Text#1716 "President Zelenskyy said on Nov 25 that Russia's strike tactics on energy infrastructure remained unchanged — hitting power lines, grids and substations to complicate electricity transmission — and called Russian aircraft, warships and weapons transports legitimate targets "
                        Text#1717 [reader-cite-ref-1748ea20ead1] " 177 " label="Source 177" (press)
                        Text#1718 " "
                        Text#1719 "."
                    View#1720
                      Text#1721 [reader-block-b100] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1722 "Reactive drone attacks were confirmed on Berezanka in Mykolaiv region and on Chornomorsk and Raukhivka in Odesa region "
                        Text#1723 [reader-cite-ref-a3c20d2359f5] " 178 " label="Source 178" (press)
                        Text#1724 "."
                    View#1725
                      Text#1726 [reader-block-b101] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1727 "A report said the Novoshakhtinsk oil refinery and a Tatarstan pumping station were burning after a Ukrainian drone attack "
                        Text#1728 [reader-cite-ref-0c5a94cefa4f] " 179 " label="Source 179" (press)
                        Text#1729 "."
                    View#1730
                      Text#1731 [reader-block-b102] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1732 "Ukraine said it struck two oil refineries in Russia's Samara region "
                        Text#1733 [reader-cite-ref-5b8b96f09b09] " 180 " label="Source 180" (press)
                        Text#1734 ". "
                        Text#1735 "In Zaporizhzhia, a Russian attack on the Kosmichnyi district injured six people, including a child, and damaged about ten private houses, a warehouse building and cars; a fire broke out on the grounds of a transport enterprise "
                        Text#1736 [reader-cite-ref-4a3d109e037d] " 181 " label="Source 181" (press)
                        Text#1737 " "
                        Text#1738 "."
                    View#1739
                      Text#1740 [reader-block-b103] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1741 "Ukrinform reported that scheduled power outages of 0.5 to 3.5 queues would run around the clock on Thursday, November 26 in parts of Ukraine "
                        Text#1742 [reader-cite-ref-02ab6bdb1476] " 182 " label="Source 182" (press)
                        Text#1743 ". "
                        Text#1744 "The government also extended the transitional deadline for businesses to provide shelters during yellow-level air alerts through June 4, 2027 "
                        Text#1745 [reader-cite-ref-3e5d3febe8ff] " 183 " label="Source 183" (press)
                        Text#1746 "."
                    View#1747
                      Text#1748 [reader-block-b104] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1749 "Ukrainian drones attacked industrial facilities in Syzran, Samara region, according to Russian authorities "
                        Text#1750 [reader-cite-ref-a79f4dfee4c6] " 184 " label="Source 184" (press)
                        Text#1751 ". "
                        Text#1752 "Separately, Ukraine's General Staff said an attack on an airfield in Russia's Nizhny Novgorod Oblast hit five Russian aircraft — three MiG-31 fighter jets and two Su-34 aircraft "
                        Text#1753 [reader-cite-ref-670c01f3dcea] " 185 " label="Source 185" (press)
                        Text#1754 " "
                        Text#1755 "."
                    View#1756
                      Text#1757 [reader-block-b105] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1758 "Ukraine's foreign minister, Andrii Sybiha, told Russian President Vladimir Putin to \"stop complaining\" about attacks on oil refineries, saying Putin could end the war if he did not like the strikes "
                        Text#1759 [reader-cite-ref-3389a231154f] " 186 " label="Source 186" (press)
                        Text#1760 "."
                    View#1761
                      Text#1762 [reader-block-b106] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1763 "Finland and Norway pledged nearly $60 million to support Ukraine's energy sector, funding equipment to repair facilities damaged by Russian attacks across the country "
                        Text#1764 [reader-cite-ref-5aa9f0082ca2] " 187 " label="Source 187" (press)
                        Text#1765 "."
                    View#1766
                      Text#1767 [reader-block-b107] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1768 "Ukrainian defense forces and the Security Service said they struck two Rosneft refineries in Samara Oblast again, noting the Syzran refinery had been hit at least a tenth time since August 2025 and the Kuibyshev refinery in Samara a fifth time "
                        Text#1769 [reader-cite-ref-3c2b800e1afa] " 188 " label="Source 188" (press)
                        Text#1770 " "
                        Text#1771 "."
                    View#1772
                      Text#1773 [reader-block-b108] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1774 "Russian shelling has again cut external power to the occupied Zaporizhzhia Nuclear Power Plant, which switched to backup generators "
                        Text#1775 [reader-cite-ref-52cfb0331384] " 189 " label="Source 189" (press)
                        Text#1776 "."
                    View#1777
                      Text#1778 [reader-block-b109] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1779 "A Ukrainian armored repair vehicle unit said it must produce 40 frontline \"korch\" vehicles monthly, noting winter has arrived and they are already working beyond capacity, and called for donations "
                        Text#1780 [reader-cite-ref-97befc8f7273] " 190 " label="Source 190" (press)
                        Text#1781 "."
                    View#1782
                      Text#1783 [reader-block-b110] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1784 "Ukraine's General Staff said its forces struck a Russian military airbase in the Nizhny Novgorod region east of Moscow "
                        Text#1785 [reader-cite-ref-0897343dcb11] " 191 " label="Source 191" (press)
                        Text#1786 "."
                    View#1787
                      Text#1788 [reader-block-b111] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1789 "Ukrinform reported that Russian forces struck a Naftogaz Group facility in Ukraine's Poltava region, forcing it to suspend operations "
                        Text#1790 [reader-cite-ref-48d193ab0faa] " 192 " label="Source 192" (press)
                        Text#1791 "."
                    View#1792
                      Text#1793 [reader-block-b112] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1794 "OSINT channel Exilenova reported preliminary reports of a crash at the \"Subhankulovo\" line production and dispatch station of Transneft-Ural in Bashkortostan, with consequences still being verified "
                        Text#1795 [reader-cite-ref-608a29b8fc00] " 193 " label="Source 193" (press)
                        Text#1796 " and posted that another unit at the Kuibyshev Oil Refinery in Samara had likely caught fire "
                        Text#1797 [reader-cite-ref-dc8dc7310e9a] " 194 " label="Source 194" (press)
                        Text#1798 ". "
                        Text#1799 "Kharkiv Oblast head Oleh Syniehubov said Russian forces attacked a civilian car with a drone in the Zolochiv hromada, killing two people "
                        Text#1800 [reader-cite-ref-c184708e9d55] " 195 " label="Source 195" (press)
                        Text#1801 ". "
                        Text#1802 "OSINT air-alert posts late on Nov 25 reported Russian drones heading toward Mykolaiv and the northern Chernihiv region in the direction of Horodnia and Snovsk "
                        Text#1803 [reader-cite-ref-8cdf64d5de8c] " 196 " label="Source 196" (press)
                        Text#1804 "."
                    View#1805
                      Text#1806 [reader-block-b113] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1807 "A Ukrainian state media report said Ukrainian forces attacked the Subhankulovo station, a key Transneft node that pumps oil from Western Siberia and Bashkortostan to refineries "
                        Text#1808 [reader-cite-ref-7d833cc909aa] " 197 " label="Source 197" (press)
                        Text#1809 "."
                    View#1810
                      Text#1811 [reader-block-b114] (contextmenu)
                        Text#1812 "OSINT channel Exilenova posted footage of what it called a successful Ukrainian FP-1 drone strike on a facility in Slovyansk in Krasnodar Krai overnight, claiming the enemy's air defense failed "
                        Text#1813 [reader-cite-ref-09ff090c3a3e] " 198 " label="Source 198" (press)
                        Text#1814 ". "
                        Text#1815 "The channel also said a fire was continuing at a key Transneft facility in Bashkortostan involved in the main oil transportation system from Western Siberia and Tatarstan "
                        Text#1816 [reader-cite-ref-e438992ae969] " 199 " label="Source 199" (press)
                        Text#1817 "."
